solution_steps:
From the given equations, we obtain the following symmetric expressions:
\begin{align*}
a(b+c) &= 152 \\
b(c+a) &= 162 \\
c(a+b) &= 170 \\
\end{align*}
Adding these equations together, we have
\begin{align*}
2(ab+bc+ca) &= 152+162+170 \\
2(ab+bc+ca) &= 484 \\
ab+bc+ca &= 242 \\
\end{align*}
We can rewrite this equation as
\begin{align*}
a(b+c) + bc &= 242 \\
152 + bc &= 242 \\
bc &= 90 \\
\end{align*}
Similarly, we can find that $ac = 80$ and $ab = 72$.
Multiplying these equations together, we have
\begin{align*}
a^2 b^2 c^2 &= (ab)(ac)(bc) \\
&= (72)(80)(90) \\
&= 518400 \\
\end{align*}
Taking the square root of both sides, we find
\begin{align*}
abc &= \sqrt{518400} \\
&= \boxed{720} \\
\end{align*}
The answer is: 720

